    "notes": "Fix of KG-2026-11-06-a (QA: one shot ran 5.3 s, total 42 s). The likely culprit was the button shot, which packed the chorus, a cricket pause and a 0.4 s hold; it is now two shots (chorus push-away, then a Megha close-up with the silent beat and bas ek). Trimmed holds and shortened the lines in shots 3, 4, 7, 8 and 9, and moved the doorbell earlier, so no shot passes about 4 s and the reel lands near 38 s with pace still over 2.3 w/s. Same game, same chip countdown, same see-it twist and mirrored button. Every house is sitting on leftover Diwali mithai and every group has a friend who says diet and eats the most, so it is one simple situation a stranger gets in 2 s. Megha (diet freak, catchphrase 'Bas ek, cheat day hai') leads; last reel was Ruhi. Game played three times: Megha 1 (ordinary), Shruti 2 for 'paise vasool' (ordinary, in character), Megha 4 more because 'kaju protein hai' (absurd). The chip counts 12, 11, 9, 3, 0, so a muted viewer always knows the stake. Claim before reveal: both celebrate 'Khatam! Ab diet shuru', then the doorbell and a see-it reveal (Avika holding two boxes). Endings tried: (1) Avika eats the last piece, no flip; (2) the host's saas sends more mithai by phone, a text twist, not see-it; (3) kept: Avika brings two more boxes and the button repeats the opening line as a chorus, then Megha's 'bas ek' loops into shot 2. Three talkers only (Megha, Shruti, Avika). Two short lines a shot, holds 0.1, pace 26 so no shot runs near 4.5 s and pace stays over 2.3 w/s."
